# Local development only. Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in what you need.
# Everything here is optional: an unset key degrades the feature that uses it,
# it never breaks the build.

# Klipy app key for GIF commenting. Read by EnvConfig and passed through to the
# spawned cc_server as CC_KLIPY_APP_KEY. Unset → the GIF picker shows a "no key"
# card. Get one from the Klipy partner panel (a test key caps at 100 calls/hour).
KLIPY_APP_KEY=

# Google OAuth client for the CLIENT-side PKCE calendar flow. This is a *public*
# iOS-type client (no secret is used) and it is NOT the same client type as the
# server-side device-code flow below. More info in @lib/features/calendar/README.md
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not .env values — listed here so the full picture lives in one place.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The SERVER resolves its own credentials in the order
# `--flag` > `CC_*` env var > baked into the release build, so to develop the
# server-side Google Calendar (device-code) flow, put these in cc_server's OWN
# environment or pass the flags:
#
#   CC_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID      / --google-client-id
#   CC_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET  / --google-client-secret
#   CC_KLIPY_APP_KEY               / --klipy-app-key
#
# The last tier of that order — what makes "use Control Center's Google app" and
# the GIF picker work with nothing configured — is baked in at RELEASE BUILD TIME
# from repository secrets by `scripts/release/builtin_credentials.sh`, which
# rewrites `packages/cc_server_core/lib/src/builtin_credentials.dart` before
# `dart build cli` (that command has no `-D` flag, so a compile-time define
# cannot reach the server binary). Those secrets are CI-only and are never read
# from a `.env`:
#
#   CC_BUILTIN_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID      Google device-code client. Both halves or
#   CC_BUILTIN_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET  neither — one alone fails the build.
#   CC_BUILTIN_KLIPY_APP_KEY
#
# A build without them (any fork, any local build) ships no built-in
# credentials: the calendar dialog asks for a client id + secret and the GIF
# picker stays hidden. Nothing confidential is eligible to be baked in — see the
# header of builtin_credentials.dart for why a Slack client secret is not.
